 "Wrestling"]]] [:script {} "$('#sports_in_same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/61/sports/'+$('#sports_in_same_games_select').val()})"] [:form {:id "other_games_form", :class "form-inline", :style "display: inline", :method "get"} [:select {:name "year", :id "sport_in_other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "Shooting in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "76"} "1875 Zappas Olympic Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "77"} "1888-89 Zappas Olympic Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "1"} "1896 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "2"} "1900 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "4"} "1906  Intercalated Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "5"} "1908 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "6"} "1912 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "7"} "1920 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "8"} "1924 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "10"} "1932 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "11"} "1936 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "12"} "1948 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "13"} "1952 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "14"} "1956 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "15"} "1960 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "16"} "1964 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "18"} "1972 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "19"} "1976 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "20"} "1980 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/SHO'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Shooting at the 2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "24 July –  2 August 2021"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "15"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2104"} "Asaka Shooting Range, Nerima, Tokyo"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "After three Olympic Games without any modifications to the shooting program, Tokyo saw significant changes. To make the shooting program gender equal, three men’s events were dropped. Not only was the men’s double trap discontinued, which had taken place between 1996 and 2016, but two of the most traditional men’s events in history were also removed. Both the 50 m small-bore rifle prone, held in every edition since 1932, and the 50 m free pistol, held in every edition since 1936, did not return in Tokyo."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Six events each for men and women were held, two each for pistols, rifles, and shotguns. In addition, three team events were added to the program. All three team events were, in fact, pairs events, as each team consisted of one woman and one man only. Nevertheless, team shooting events returned to the Olympic program after 97 years, having been discontinued after the 1924 Olympics and, of course, they were the first ever Olympic mixed gender shooting events. For further gender equality, the formats of the events were changed, with all events using the same format and the same number of shots. The only remaining small difference was the caliber between the sporting pistol used by women and the rapid-fire pistol used by men."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The qualification phase started with the 2018 World Shooting Championships (held in Changwon, Korea) on 2 September 2018 and then continued through various continental championships, the 2019 World Cup, and some multi-sport games. Originally, the qualification process ended in March 2020 but, due to the postponement of the Tokyo Olympics to 2021, some additional spots were awarded up to June 2021. The places were not won personally for athletes but for nations, so that the shooters who secured the place did not always take part in Tokyo. Unlike former Olympics, the host nation Japan was given a quota spot for every individual event. In total 360 shooters qualified, of whom 355 (178 men and 177 women) actually competed. These shooters represented 101 NOCs and, for the first time ever, more women from different NOCs (73) than men (66) competed."] "\n\n" [:p {} "With her ninth participation at the Olympics, having not missed any Games since her first participation in 1988, " [:a {:href "/athletes/42492"} "Nino Salukvadze"] " equalled the record held by " [:a {:href "/athletes/43227"} "Afanasijs Kuzmins"] " for shooters. Salukvadze competed in the 10 m air pistol event along with " [:a {:href "/athletes/41415"} "Mariya Grozdeva"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/43353"} "Otryadyn Gündegmaa"] ", who both participated in their seventh Games. Salukvadze’s ninth Olympic appearance was also an Olympic best for females, in any sport."] "\n\n" [:p {} "A total of 19 different nations won shooting medals at Tokyo. For the first time since 2004, however, the host nation did not win a medal in shooting events. With " [:a {:href "/athletes/2502763"} "Zhang Changhong"] " winning gold in the men’s 50 m small-bore rifle three positions, China topped the medal standings again after also being on top from 2000-08, while Iran, San Marino, and Serbia won their first ever shooting medals (Serbian shooters had already won medals before but for " [:a {:href "/countries/YUG"} "Yugoslavia"] " and " [:a {:href "/countries/SCG"} "Serbia and Montenegro"] ", respectively). This was also San Marino’s first ever Olympic medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The most decorated shooter in Tokyo was " [:a {:href "/athletes/131606"} "Vitalina Batsarashkina"] ", who won two golds and one silver. The only other shooter winning two gold medals was " [:a {:href "/athletes/141760"} "Yang Qian"] ", with no male shooter winning more than one gold medal. With a total of three shooting medals, Batsarashkina became the first shooter to win three medals at the same Games since 1924 and, of course, was the first female shooter to do so."] "\n\n" [:p {} "An age record for female shooters was set at these Games by " [:a {:href "/athletes/145213"} "Anna Dulce"] " of Moldova, born on 22 October 2005, as she was only aged 15 years 276 days when participating in the women’s 10 m air rifle event. She surpassed " [:a {:href "/athletes/41680"} "Mladenka Maleniča"] ", who was 16-115 in her first event in 1988. Another age record was set in Tokyo by " [:a {:href "/athletes/141876"} "Sheng Lihao"] ", born on 4 December 2004, who became the youngest ever Olympic shooting medallist, aged 16 years 233 days when winning silver in the men’s 10 m air rifle event."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/18000720"} "Air Pistol, 10 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "24 July 2021"] "\n" [:td {} "36"] "\n" [:td {} "29"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/18000723"} "Rapid-Fire Pistol, 25 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "1 –  2 August 2021"] "\n" [:td {} "27"] "\n" [:td {} "19"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/18000728"} "Air Rifle, 10 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "25 July 2021"] "\n